    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0434" n="400" xml:id="pg400"/>

                <p>[Indorsements.]</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters Department of Dakota,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Paul</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Minnesota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1870-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 3, 1870.</date></p>
                <p>Respectfully forwarded to the Adjutant General of the Army, through headquarters
                    Military Division of the Missouri.</p>
                <p>The papers in reference to the survey of Fort Wadsworth reservation have been
                    forwarded in another communication. Captain Heap was instructed to mark out the
                    line in front of the position of Fort Geo. H. Thomas, for the information of the
                    troops.</p>
                <p>Since that country is likely to increase in importance, it would be advantageous
                    if the 49th parallel were authoritatively established, and with a view of
                    suggesting such a result, this communication is transmitted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WINF’D S. HANCOCK, <hi rendition="#italic">Major General U. S. A</hi>.,
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>



